UNEP International Resource Panel, 2013. Report by M. A. Reuter, C. Hudson, A. van Schaik, K. Heiskanen, C. Meskers, and C. Hagelüken. Metal Recycling: Opportunities, Limits, Infrastructure, 320 pages. ISBN 9789280732672. [Official complete report](https://wedocs.unep.org/handle/20.500.11822/8423).

Read the entire report for a substantial product-to-process and recovery-infrastructure study. Reconstruct material/element flows, thermodynamic and technological limits, product complexity, collection/separation/refining interfaces, quality, and system dependencies. Distinguish dated quantitative observations from general physical arguments and later evidence.

The official record identifies the full report, distinguished from its smaller summary/factsheet. The work permits attributed educational/nonprofit reproduction under its stated conditions; commercial reuse needs separate permission, and component rights remain relevant. Metadata, full-report route, and rights context checked on 29 October 2026. No book, product dataset, or images are bundled.

